   "text": {
    "L1": "We measure capacity in millilitres and litres.",
    "L2": "The key fact is that 1 litre equals 1000 millilitres.",
    "L3": "Before comparing, change both amounts to the same unit. So 1 litre is more than 500 millilitres.",
    "L4": "Do not compare only the numbers 1 and 500. Compare 1000 millilitres with 500 millilitres.",
    "L5": "A taller container does not always hold more. Capacity depends on height and width together.",
    "L6": "The same 500 millilitres can look higher in a tall thin bottle, but the amount stays the same.",
    "L7": "To find how many glasses fill a jug, count how many times the glass amount fits. Four 250 millilitre glasses make 1000 millilitres, or 1 litre.",
    "L8": "Now tap the container that holds more than 500 millilitres."
   },
